That the Board take the following action concerning the State Housing Initiatives Partnership (SHIP) Local Housing Assistance Plan (LHAP):
A. Rescind its action of September 4, 2025, CAR II-2, adopting the 2025–2028 SHIP LHAP, SHIP Certification, and associated Resolution;
B. Adopt the Escambia County 2025–2028 State Housing Initiatives Partnership (SHIP) Local Housing Assistance Plan (LHAP), including SHIP-financed affordable housing strategies, specified eligibility and beneficiary definitions, maximum SHIP award limitations, fiscal and administrative provisions, descriptions of affordable housing incentives, annual program service delivery goals, and SHIP certification;
C. Adopt a Resolution approving the LHAP as required by the State Housing Initiatives Partnership Program Act, Florida Statutes 420.907-420.9079, and Chapter 67-37, Florida Administrative Code; authorizing the Chairman and County Administrator to execute any necessary documents and certifications; authorizing the submission of the Local Housing Assistance Plan for review and approval by the Florida Housing Finance Corporation; and providing an effective date;
D. Approve the Certification to Florida Housing Finance Corporation (Exhibit D) of the LHAP;
E. Authorize staff to make minor revisions to the Fiscal Year 2025–2028 SHIP budgetary allocations and the LHAP to accurately reflect current funding distributions provided by the Florida Housing Finance Corporation (FHFC), if required for final review;
F. Authorize the County Administrator, as appropriate, to sign additional documents required to submit, receive, and implement the SHIP LHAP and all related activities; and
G. Authorize the Chair to sign the Resolution and Certification to FHFC for the Escambia County 2025–2028 SHIP LHAP.

